<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Sint Eustatius</h1><p class="st-meta">1636 CE – 1845 CE · capital Oranjestad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tiny Dutch island that became the busiest free port of the 18th-century Caribbean and gave the first foreign salute to the flag of the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-zeeland">Zeeland</a> settlers founded a colony on Sint Eustatius in 1636 and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-oranje-sint-eustatius">Fort Oranje</a> above the harbour at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oranjestad-sint-eustatius">Oranjestad</a>. The island changed hands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, English and French many times in the 17th century before settling under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>With little farmland, Statia thrived as a neutral free port where goods of every nation were traded, including arms, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and enslaved people. Its Lower Town was lined with warehouses, and the island had a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-reformed-church">Dutch Reformed</a> church, a Jewish congregation and a polyglot merchant class. On 16 November 1776 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-oranje-sint-eustatius">Fort Oranje</a> returned the salute of the American brig <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-doria">Andrew Doria</a>, the first recognition of the new republic's flag.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> declared war on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1780, and Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-brydges-rodney-1st-baron-rodney">George Rodney</a> seized and plundered the island in 1781. Its trade never recovered. After further occupations, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule was restored in 1816, and in 1845 the island was placed under the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-curacao">Curaçao and Dependencies</a>. It is now a special municipality of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sint-eustatius.jpg" alt="Sint Eustatius" width="320" height="211"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sint_Eustatius_from_ISS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1636 CE – 1845 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Oranjestad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Johannes de Graaff</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Church</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Statia, Dutch Sint Eustatius</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1740&amp;focus=sint-eustatius" aria-label="Sint Eustatius on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2969 1529 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sint Eustatius lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3289 1785L5097 634M3289 1785L3106 1982"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5097 634h0M3106 1982h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3289 1785h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3289 1785h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Oranjestad. <a href="/atlas?year=1740&amp;focus=sint-eustatius">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
